        <title type="html"><![CDATA[There are more keydowns that don't constitute user activation #41393]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42337</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42337"/>
        <updated>2025-12-10T04:03:22.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161916643?u=ac460ddbb1c07a3453efc41c8bbb87d21b4878a5&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">The current documentation states that all keydown events count as user activation except the Esc key and browser-reserved shortcut keys.<br>
However, in practice, several additional keys do not trigger user activation in major browsers (Chrome, Firefox), such as CapsLock, NumLock, and other lock/system keys.</p>
<p dir="auto">This update clarifies that user activation is not triggered by certain non-character or system keys, making the documentation more accurate and aligned with real browser behavior.</p>
<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/161916643/524629710-6e25b448-e531-4f77-85ad-78fac0f4a6f7.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3NjU0MTY4NTgsIm5iZiI6MTc2NTQxNjU1OCwicGF0aCI6Ii8xNjE5MTY2NDMvNTI0NjI5NzEwLTZlMjViNDQ4LWU1MzEtNGY3Ny04NWFkLTc4ZmFjMGY0YTZmNy5wbmc_.V6ZarPjdNZkEyY74OUadZva2xHfk76Kze2HGoWxJ-LA"><img width="728" height="113" alt="image" src="https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/161916643/524629710-6e25b448-e531-4f77-85ad-78fac0f4a6f7.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3NjU0MTY4NTgsIm5iZiI6MTc2NTQxNjU1OCwicGF0aCI6Ii8xNjE5MTY2NDMvNTI0NjI5NzEwLTZlMjViNDQ4LWU1MzEtNGY3Ny04NWFkLTc4ZmFjMGY0YTZmNy5wbmc_.V6ZarPjdNZkEyY74OUadZva2xHfk76Kze2HGoWxJ-LA" style="max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 113px;"></a>]]></content>
